# Forms

Interactive forms use **react-hook-form** + **Zod** (`zodResolver`). Layout/a11y use `@/components/ui/field`. Context wiring uses `@/components/ui/form`.

## Stack

- Schema: Zod (share with `next-safe-action` `.inputSchema` when the same shape hits the server)
- Form state: `useForm` + `zodResolver`
- Provider: `<Form {...form}>` (`FormProvider`) so fields never take `control`
- Fields: reusable components with `FormField` + `useFormContext` — not inline `useState`
- Markup: `Field`, `FieldLabel`, `FieldError`, `FieldGroup`, `FieldDescription`

## Pattern

```tsx
"use client"

import { zodResolver } from "@hookform/resolvers/zod"
import { useForm } from "react-hook-form"
import { z } from "zod"

import { Form } from "@/components/ui/form"
import { FieldGroup } from "@/components/ui/field"
import { EmailField } from "@/components/forms/email-field" // reusable

const schema = z.object({ email: z.email() })

export function InviteForm() {
  const form = useForm<z.infer<typeof schema>>({
    resolver: zodResolver(schema),
    defaultValues: { email: "" },
  })

  return (
    <Form {...form}>
      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit((data) => { /* call safe action */ })}>
        <FieldGroup>
          <EmailField />
        </FieldGroup>
      </form>
    </Form>
  )
}
```

Reusable field (no `control` prop):

```tsx
"use client"

import { FormField } from "@/components/ui/form"
import { Field, FieldError, FieldLabel } from "@/components/ui/field"
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input"

export function EmailField() {
  return (
    <FormField
      name="email"
      render={({ field, fieldState }) => (
        <Field data-invalid={fieldState.invalid}>
          <FieldLabel htmlFor={field.name}>Email</FieldLabel>
          <Input {...field} id={field.name} type="email" aria-invalid={fieldState.invalid} />
          {fieldState.invalid && <FieldError errors={[fieldState.error]} />}
        </Field>
      )}
    />
  )
}
```

## Rules

- Put shared fields under `src/components/forms/`
- Set `data-invalid` on `Field` and `aria-invalid` on the control
- Prefer `FormField` over prop-drilling `control` or bare `Controller`
- Do not manage field values with `useState`
